# {{product}} docs & skill — setup guide

Companion to the package `README.md`: layout, install options, daily use, other agents, the code graph, keeping the docs current, troubleshooting.

## 1. Package layout

```
{{package_name}}/
├── README.md            start here (people + agent setup instructions)
├── website/             documentation website: open website/index.html
└── repo-kit/            installed next to the code
    ├── AGENTS.md        rules every coding agent follows
    ├── CLAUDE.md        Claude Code instructions (merged into an existing one)
    ├── SETUP-GUIDE.md   this guide
    ├── codebase-docs.json   documentation project settings (source root, adapters …)
    ├── mkdocs.yml       website build configuration
    ├── .claude/skills/{{skill_name}}/SKILL.md   the Claude Code skill
    └── {{docs_dir}}/    pages, sources (_src), research notes (_notes), tools (_tools), agent index (agent/), llms.txt
```

Not included: the graphify code graph (large; its paths point at the machine that built it). Build it on the real repository (§5).

**Sensitive**: {{sensitive_note}} No passwords or keys are included anywhere.

## 2. Prerequisites

| Need | For | Check |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Claude Code (desktop or CLI) | the skill | `claude --version` |
| Python 3.9+ | `lookup.py`, docs tools | `python --version` |
| `pip install mkdocs-material` (optional) | rebuilding the website | `python -m mkdocs --version` |
| graphify (optional) | code-graph queries | `graphify --help` |

## 3. Install

Give an AI agent `README.md` ("Read README.md in this folder and set up the {{product}} docs skill"); it follows the setup instructions there. By hand:

- **Into the code repository (recommended)**: copy the contents of `repo-kit/` into the repository root (the folder containing {{markers_text}}); append `repo-kit/CLAUDE.md` to an existing `CLAUDE.md`. Commit to a private branch; add `site/` and `graphify-out/` to `.gitignore`.
- **Docs only**: unzip anywhere, copy `repo-kit/.claude/skills/{{skill_name}}/SKILL.md` to `<unzipped>/.claude/skills/{{skill_name}}/SKILL.md`, open Claude Code in the unzipped folder. Answers then come from the docs only.
- **Personal / global**: copy `SKILL.md` to `~/.claude/skills/{{skill_name}}/` and replace `PINNED_DOCS_ROOT: none` with the absolute docs root.

Claude Code discovers skills at session start: open a new session, type `/` and look for `{{skill_name}}`.

## 4. Daily use

Ask normally (the skill triggers on {{product}} topics) or force it with `/{{skill_name}} <question>`. The agent reads `llms.txt`, looks names up, reads the page and the reference entry, verifies in the code and cites clickable `file:line` links; change requests end with a *File · What to change · Why* table.

Lookups by hand (run from the workspace root):

```bash
python {{docs_dir}}/_tools/lookup.py "{{verify_name}}"
```

```bash
python {{docs_dir}}/_tools/lookup.py "{{verify_name}}" --find "<text in its source file>"
```

Other agents: Codex, Cursor and other AGENTS.md-aware tools read `AGENTS.md` automatically; for GitHub Copilot copy it into `.github/copilot-instructions.md`.

## 5. Code graph (optional)

```bash
uv tool install "graphifyy[sql,openai]"
```

```bash
graphify extract . --code-only
```

```bash
graphify cluster-only . --no-label
```

```bash
graphify export wiki
```

Then `graphify query "<question>"`, `graphify explain "<Name>"`, `graphify path "<A>" "<B>"`, `graphify affected "<Name>"`. Keep it current with `graphify update .` or `graphify hook install` (git hooks).

## 6. Keeping the docs current

With the `codebase-documenter` skill installed: *"/codebase-documenter update-docs"*. Without it, from the repository root (set `DOCS_SOURCE_ROOT=.`):

```bash
python {{docs_dir}}/_tools/build_docs.py
```

```bash
python {{docs_dir}}/_tools/gen_agent_index.py
```

```bash
python -m mkdocs build
```

Edit narrative sources in `{{docs_dir}}/_src/` only; reference pages are regenerated by the skill's adapters.

## 7. Troubleshooting

| Problem | Fix |
| --- | --- |
| Skill not in the `/` list | Start Claude Code in the folder that holds `.claude/skills/`; check the front matter; new session |
| Printed paths don't open | Run `lookup.py` from the workspace root by its path; don't `cd` into the docs |
| `source root: NOT FOUND` | `--src <path>` or set `DOCS_SOURCE_ROOT` |
| Garbled characters on Windows | Python 3.9+; or `set PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8` |
| MkDocs warnings after edits | `build_docs.py` lists unresolved link tags |
